m('02-alkenes-and-addition','Alkenes and addition reactions',p('Series and structure','C=C functional group, unsaturated.','CₙH₂ₙ for acyclic one-double-bond series.','Ethene, propene, butene, pentene.','Every carbon has four bonds total.'),p('Displayed formulas','Show every atom and bond.','C=C counts as two bonds.','Ethene CH₂=CH₂, propene CH₂=CHCH₃.','Retain the rest of any longer chain.'),p('Hydrogen addition','Heated nickel catalyst.','Add H to each former double-bond carbon.','C=C changes into C–C.','Ethene becomes ethane.'),p('Steam addition','Elevated temperature/pressure, acid catalyst.','H and OH add across C=C.','Ethene becomes ethanol.','Products depend on supplied structure/conditions.'),p('Halogen addition','Cl₂, Br₂ or I₂ adds across double bond.','One halogen on each former C=C carbon.','Ethene +Br₂: CH₂BrCH₂Br.','No missing atoms or unchanged double bond.'),p('Tests and combustion','Bromine water orange to colourless.','Alkane remains coloured in ordinary test.','Alkenes often burn smokily in air.','Complete combustion still yields CO₂ and water.')),
m('03-alcohols-acids-and-esters','Alcohols, carboxylic acids and esters',p('Alcohol family','–OH functional group.','Methanol, ethanol, propanol, butanol.','Uses: fuels/solvents; ethanol in drinks.','Methanol is toxic, not drinkable.'),p('Alcohol reactions','Sodium: hydrogen and sodium compound.','Complete combustion: carbon dioxide/water.','Small members dissolve to varying extents.','Primary examples oxidise to carboxylic acids.'),p('Fermentation','Sugar +yeast, warm and anaerobic.','Ethanol and carbon dioxide form.','Excess heat denatures enzymes/kills yeast.','Dilute product needs separation.'),p('Compare production','Fermentation: renewable crop input, land/time needs.','Ethene hydration: steam, acid catalyst, high T/P.','Often continuous, finite petrochemical feedstock.','Compare purity, yield, energy, cost and land.'),p('Carboxylic acids','–COOH functional group.','Methanoic, ethanoic, propanoic, butanoic.','Partial ionisation: weak acid, not necessarily dilute.','Carbonates give salt, water and CO₂.'),p('Esters','Carboxylic acid +alcohol →ester +water.','Ethanol +ethanoic acid: ethyl ethanoate.','Ester link –C(=O)–O–.','Condensation, often acid-catalysed.')),
m('04-polymer-structures','Addition and condensation polymers',p('Monomers and chains','Monomer: small joining molecule.','Polymer: long repeating chain.','Keep side groups and atom counts.','Functional groups determine joining.'),p('Addition unit','Ethene double bond opens.',visual={'kind':'remaining-chem-polymer','after':0}),p('Other addition units','Poly(propene): –CH₂–CH(CH₃)–.','Single backbone bonds, outward links, brackets, n.','Restore C=C to find monomer.','No small molecule eliminated.'),p('Condensation','Monomers have two reactive functional groups.','Groups join and eliminate a small molecule.','Usually water by-product.','Some monomer atoms leave the polymer.'),p('Polyesters','Diol: two –OH groups.','Diacid: two –COOH groups.','Ester links repeatedly connect them.','Two joining sites allow extended chains.'),p('Avoid drawing errors','Do not keep C=C in addition backbone.','Do not remove methyl or halogen side groups.','Chain bonds pass through both brackets.','One alcohol +one acid forms a small ester.')),
